      "name": null,
      "problem": "Calculate the $x$-intercept of the line $y=-2x+10.$",
      "worked_solution": "At the $x$-intercept, the $y$-coordinate is equal to $0.$ So, we can substitute $y=0$ into the equation and then solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2x+10 \\\\ 0 & =-2x+10 \\\\ 2x & =10 \\\\ x & =\\frac{10}{2} \\\\ x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercept is $x=5.$ The coordinates of the $x$-intercept are $(5,0).$",
